think The crash root, one line for two loops: tools/hooks/pre-commit invoked its pin scan as a literal /bin/sh -- itself the 20260828 repair for a jail whose PATH sh was the macOS selector wrapper -- and the 20260829 Codex jail denies that wrapper's read of /private/var/select/sh, garbling the scan's opening substitution-plus-cd. Mystery's finished lap died at the signer; Mind proved the repair from both sides (explicit bash, same scan, verdict=ok in the same jail) and parked at custody. The fix: the hook now probes /bin/bash, bash, /bin/sh in order, each candidate proving the exact failing shape (a substitution, a CDPATH-clean cd, a pwd) before trust, and both scan call sites plus the refusal message run under the probed scan_shell variable. Proven: syntax clean under both interpreters, the probe picks /bin/bash here, both interpreters answer the live scan identically, and tools/p/pin_bound_touch_witness.rish arms the repaired hook in real pens -- 36 cases GREEN. Booked REDS %348, CLOSED, fetch-first (the peer's 52c49cecb landed no row, so %348 was free).
